imagine you have a looker dashboard  filled with useful data and insights  many of your users will find the  dashboard helpful and use it often  but your users spend most of their time  on existing applications and workflows  how can your dashboard reach your users  in their current context  well  embed the dashboard into your existing  applications so your user can act on  data insights without leaving their app  or disrupting their workflows  hi  welcome to our video series on embedding  looker i'm jeremy a developer relations  engineer at looker  in this video we will explore the  multiple ways you can embed your local  content via iframes  [Music]  there are three options for embedding  via iframe  private embedding  sso single sign-on embedding and sso  embedding with the embed sdk  let's do a quick overview of each iframe  embedding option and how your host  application can interact and communicate  with your iframe by the way a quick  knowledge check  for the rest of this video we assume you  have a basic knowledge of javascript and  the iframe html element  first  let's introduce you to the private  embedding option  let's look at your host applications dom  you create an iframe inside the dom  then you take a modified url of your  looker content and set it on your iframe  source attribute  and now you have embedded liquor content  in your iframe  keep in mind for this option your user  must log into looker via your admin's  chosen authentication mechanism  the user's looker account must have the  right permissions to access the embedded  content so  consider private embedding if you need a  quick and easy embedding option and your  user can log into your liquor instance  but what if you want your host  application to control user  authentication and  authorization for example your user  authenticates with an identity provider  connected to your host application  all separate from your looker instance  then try out our ssl embedding option  again you create an iframe in your host  application  but this time  you point the iframe source attribute to  a unique  one-time use url that you must generate  for each embed user session this  one-time use url sets the content access  permissions of the session  the url logs in your user as an existing  looker embed user or creates a new one  with the content access permissions  consider the sso embedding option if  your host application controls user  authentication and authorization  next  let's look at the sso embedding with the  embed sdk option  this is our recommended embedding option  it's the same as the previously  mentioned sso embedding option however  your host application does not directly  manage the iframe  instead your host application calls the  javascript embed sdk to create and  manage the iframe  just like i described for the previous  sso embedding option you must still  generate a unique url for every embed  user session  but the embed sdk with our accompanying  code samples partly automates the url  generation and manages the iframe for  you we recommend this option the most  because of the embed sdk's convenient  javascript api and ease of use lastly  let's look at how your host application  can communicate with your iframe to make  your embedded content more interactive  your iframe and host application can  communicate with each other with all the  previous embedding options  your iframe emits an event when its  state changes for example when a  dashboard finishes loading  your host application can listen to  these events  and react accordingly  also your host application can send  messages to the iframe to change the  iframe state like telling the iframe to  load a new dashboard  if you use the embed sdk  then your host application calls the  sdk's javascript api to listen to events  and send messages to the iframe  but if you do not use the embed sdk  then your host application will use the  window interface to listen to events  and send messages to the iframe  in conclusion you can embed liquid  content in an iframe in multiple ways  depending on your needs  and your host application can interact  with the iframe  if you don't know where to start  we recommend getting started with  private embedding because it is our  simplest embedding option  and then we recommend you get started  with the sso embedding with the embed  sdk to help you get more familiar with  embedding looker and with that  you will soon be an expert in embedding  looker so check out our developer portal  linked in the description below and get  started embedding your liquor content  also stay tuned for future videos in  this series where we'll walk you through  how to embed looker in more detail  see you next time  [Music]  you
 

